<title>USA: Russellville, Ark., voters defeat $7.5 mln bond.</title>
<headline>Russellville, Ark., voters defeat $7.5 mln bond.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russellville, Ark., voters Tuesday soundly defeated a proposed $7.5 million bond issue for various capital improvements including a new police station.</p>
<p>Turnout was light, with just 15 percent of the city's registered voters hitting the polls, according to the Pope County Clerk's office.</p>
<p>The results are still uncertified, Sharla Reddell, a deputy clerk there said.</p>
<p>Early results are as follows:</p>
<p>--Fire station improvement bonds, 715 for, 1,449 against.</p>
<p>--Police station improvement bonds, 760 for, 1,399 against.</p>
<p>--Park and recreation improvement bonds, 870 for, 1,313 against.</p>
<p>--City hall improvement bonds, 564 for, 1,583 against.</p>
<p>--Airport improvement bonds, 521 for, 1,624 against.</p>
<p>--Kathie O'Donnell, 212-859-1655</p>
</text>
